\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{An integral pairing on the quaternion lattice}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [Hurwitz order](fgap-0016) contains
#{h=(1+\qi +\qj +\qk)/2}. Its usual rational Euclidean
pairing has #{\langle 1,h\rangle=1/2}, so this norm pairing
cannot be evaluated integrally on every pair of lattice
vectors. A coefficient form over #{\mathbb Z} must have
integer values and an invertible integral Gram matrix.
Which invariant form on this lattice has those properties?}
